//  numbers in its car family (if you have run it), otherwise from the general one; computed, not learned; the community
//  is added on top; and a category already run keeps its own. With the PRODUCTION data (the families
//  come from the catalog).


// 09/09 (performance of the ) — THE INCUMBENT CACHE CHANGES NOT A SINGLE FACTOR: for the whole cohort of a
//  production series, CohortCandidateFactors with the precomputed set gives exactly the same as with the sweep.


// 09/09 (performance of the ) — THE StayingDrivers MEMO IS EXACT AND BITES: same answer as the count without
//  memo with the world seated; after a contract expires (seat_contract_start: the key covers it), after opening a
//  seat and after retiring someone it still equals the count without the memo; and with the same inputs the second call
//  comes back through the memo with the same answer.


// 09/09 (performance) — THE DATA MEMORY OF SeatsForClass IS EXACT: for all live series, with the world
//  seated, with an open seat and with a person moved, the version with memory gives seat by seat the same
//  as the version without it (label, occupant, level, livery, open); and it survives a ReplaceSeries (the epoch
//  empties the memory).


// Port 0.7.0 (F22) — THE DATA EPOCH REALLY RISES, AND WITH IT THE TWO MEMOS EXPIRE.
//
// In f0 the key of these memos carries `AffinityEpoch()`, which lives in `career_affinity` (contracts) and does not
// exist here; 0.7.0 puts `DataEpoch()` in its place, which rises in `InvalidateCalendarProjectionCache` (that is, in
// LoadSeries / ReplaceSeries / LoadSeriesCalendar / ReplaceCalendar) and at the close of `LoadSeasonData`. This test
// exists because a PINNED epoch compiles, breaks no memo on its own and leaves five team-name tests
// red without saying why -- that is how it was measured in the port lab.
//
// What is set up is exactly the hole the epoch plugs: the catalog is changed WITHOUT moving the signature of the
// data memory (`SeatsDataFirma` counts series, fields, pinned and roster, and here the four numbers
// stay the same). If the memo did not look at the epoch, it would answer with the previous world.


