// Academy pipeline: the ramp-up rule — the contest (cohort) only bites on aspirational seats
// (works, or a series above your phase); the on-ramp (open at your level/below) never faces a contest.
static void test_disputa_cantera_ramp() {
    using namespace market;
    // `works` gets DROPPED as a gate, per the user's decision. That field did TWO jobs: how
    // you get in (you sign up or get signed) and whether you have to win the spot from someone. In reality the second
    // depends on how FAR ABOVE you they are, not on a per-class label: at the base, anyone who shows up gets a seat.
    // Formula Vee came out "closed" and Karting "open" without answering to anything real, and that
    // left the rookie shut out of a category at THEIR OWN LEVEL. Now a seat at your level is yours whether it's run
    // by a factory team or not; `works` still decides the reputation bar and the contract type.
    CHECK(!SeatIsAspirational(true, 3, 5));   // works BELOW your phase -> on-ramp, not contested
    CHECK(!SeatIsAspirational(true, 5, 5));   // works AT your level -> also yours
    CHECK(SeatIsAspirational(true, 6, 5));    // works ABOVE -> now that one is contested
    // open ABOVE your phase -> aspirational
    CHECK(SeatIsAspirational(false, 6, 5));
    // open at your level -> ON-RAMP: not aspirational (no contest)
    CHECK(!SeatIsAspirational(false, 5, 5));
    // open BELOW your level -> ON-RAMP: not aspirational
    CHECK(!SeatIsAspirational(false, 2, 5));
}

// Academy pipeline: the COHORT branch of SeatsForClass labels every seat with FeederTeamFor(class,
// livery[i]) as FIRST precedence (above the classTeams / fictional-pool fallback), indexing seat<->
// livery via LiveriesForClass(cls). With the map NOT loaded (back-compat) it falls back to the previous precedence.


// Academy pipeline (plus a fix after review): consistency of the team<->skin binding.
// The UNIVERSAL guarantee is FUNCTIONAL IDENTITY livery->team: both the market (SeatsForClass) and the track
// (ComposeSeasonGrid) resolve a livery's team via the SAME FeederTeamFor, so a given livery ALWAYS
// belongs to the same team. Index-based alignment (grid[i].livery == seats[i].livery) only holds in
// academy classes WITHOUT driver_liveries binding; classes WITH binding (fvee/drift_championship_2323/aurora_masters_1380/...) place the
// real driver's brand livery at a different position -> they diverge by index BY DESIGN (it's not an inconsistency in the
// team<->skin binding, they just index differently). That's why the per-index check (B) is scoped to a class WITHOUT binding.


// seat occupancy round-trips through the additive save (the SAVE round-trip was added
// earlier — those CHECKs PASS) AND SeatsForClass REFLECTS the persisted occupancy: a seat_occupant
// entry keyed "<series>#<idx>" overrides that seat's occupant. The test loads the series/roster/equiv data.


// CALENDAR side: RolloverYearReport records per-team OPEN seats (granularity, not just a
// tier count). A retirement marks the retiree's SPECIFIC team seat open (kSeatOpen sentinel in seat_occupant);
// a fully-occupied class (no retiree among its occupants) has NO open seat; a promoted climber re-occupies a
// freed seat at his destination tier (the open set stays consistent with PromoteFreedSeats). Uses ReplaceRoster
// (the test_e3_rollover_report idiom) to inject a deterministic tier-1 retiree + climber.


// MARKET side: GenerateOffers is driven by OPEN seats across all tiers. A retirement at any
// tier -> that team's seat appears as an offer; a fully-occupied CLOSED class produces NO offer; era-memory
// excluded; determinism preserved. The open-seat source is the seat_occupant the rollover populated.
// a fully-occupied OPEN class (privateer/customer grid) is EXEMPT from this gate — it always
// advertises a seat — so (a) below now asserts BOTH halves: CLOSED stays gated, OPEN doesn't.


// a class WITHOUT curated real teams (cohort/generation) must NOT collapse every seat to a
// single shared cohort DRIVER name as the "team" ("Luz Verdano" xN). With the fictional pool loaded, each seat
// gets a DETERMINISTIC pool name keyed by (series|seat) so DISTINCT series get DISTINCT labels. Pool EMPTY (not
// loaded) -> the legacy homage/name fallback (no regression). Leaves the pool CLEARED so later tests keep the
// legacy behavior (order-independent).


// RELEVANCE BAND. The bypass ("an OPEN series ALWAYS advertises even with no
// seat freed up") is gated to a band: an OPEN series with no freed seat doesn't advertise if its tier is more than
// MK_OFFER_BAND_BELOW below your phase (a GT3 isn't courted by karting). A genuinely FREED seat surfaces at
// ANY tier (a won vacancy != spam). (a) harbor_trophy_6546 (tier 1) at phase 5 with no freed seat -> does NOT offer;
// (b) the SAME one with a freed seat -> offers (band skipped); (c) series within the band keep offering.


// an OPEN series (open grid, customer car) ALWAYS advertises a seat within its
// offer window, even if the roster leaves it 100% occupied — unlike a CLOSED one (factory seat),
// which still requires an open seat/displacement (unchanged). harbor_trophy_6546 (tier 1, class
// Falcon_Cup_6341 = grid_kind "open" in classes.json, NOT listed in series_access.psv -> closed=false by default)
// is the tier-1 OPEN series used by test_open_seat_offers; its round 1 opens on day-of-year 55 (series_calendar.psv),
